WEBVTT

00:00:00.876 --> 00:00:04.736
Create the customer with a name and contact information.

00:00:04.736 --> 00:00:07.789
The customer is the billing relationship.

00:00:07.789 --> 00:00:14.079
Our fictional example is Cedar Grove Market, with one service location and one assembly.

00:00:31.065 --> 00:00:37.413
Choose the tester and calibrated gauge, set the appointment date, and confirm the relevant form.

00:00:37.413 --> 00:00:40.860
The recording uses a fixed scenario date.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:46.320
In your workspace, use the actual appointment and check any scheduling warnings.

00:01:01.497 --> 00:01:08.331
Choose the result and record the device readings, performed date and time, and any field notes.

00:01:08.331 --> 00:01:11.331
These are fictional training values.

00:01:11.331 --> 00:01:16.502
Use the actual measurements and required procedure for your device and authority.

00:01:31.804 --> 00:01:36.915
Open the exact approved PDF and inspect the fictional training report.

00:01:36.915 --> 00:01:42.559
The same approved revision is the one attached when preparing the municipality submission.

00:02:02.291 --> 00:02:08.560
From the approved test, create an invoice linked to the customer, location, and test.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:13.784
Confirm the service description, price, issue date, and due date.

00:02:13.784 --> 00:02:18.297
This link lets the submission workflow check payment eligibility.
